 /* Start the next queued frame if the IN endpoint is idle. ud.lock held. */
+/*
+ * NCM framing (CDC-NCM 1.0, section 3): the bulk endpoints carry NTBs, not
+ * bare Ethernet frames.  An NTB16 is a 12-byte header, then NDP16 descriptors
+ * that say where each datagram sits, then the datagrams, all padded to a
+ * 4-byte boundary.
+ *
+ *   NTB header (12 bytes, little endian)
+ *     0  wNDPIndex       offset of the first NDP, from the NTB start
+ *     4  wHeaderLength   length of the NTB header
+ *     6  wSequence       wraps at 65535
+ *     8  wBlockLength    whole NTB length
+ *    10  wFpIndex        offset of the datagram area (0xffff = no padding)
+ *
+ *   NDP16 entry (8 bytes per datagram, plus a 4-byte terminator)
+ *     0  wDatagramIndex  offset of the datagram from the NTB start
+ *     2  wDatagramLength
+ *     4  wNextNdpIndex   offset of the next NDP, 0 = last
+ *
+ * Only the send direction is framed: this link carries the console, so the
+ * phone transmits and the host does not have to answer.
